    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nEssentially, I copy and paste paths from a failing test. I simply copy the path and use Telescope to search for the file. However, when I attempted to switch to `mini.pick` and tried to paste it didn't populate the prompt with the clipboard content and search the file path.\n\nCould you please add the functionality or if it already exists can you please point it out? Thanks for all the work around the mini.nvim world 🎖 ",
