        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> I meant with default mappings (so don't change `mappings.paste`, just a simple `require('mini.pick').setup()`):\n> \n> * Start a picker. For example, with `:Pick files`.\n> * Press `<C-r>` and then press `+`. This will append contents of the system clipboard to the current query.\n> \n> > Also, is it possible to support 2 keys? My use case is that I have a Linux and a Mac machine, so I'd like to use cmd-r for Mac and C-r for Linux PC.\n> \n> The `<C-r>` mapping is chosen as it mimics the same behavior from Neovim. See `:h i_CTRL-R`. I'd suggest using the same mapping here also.\n> \n> But to answer the question, the currently supported are only single character. More precisely, everything supported by `:h strgetchar()` will probably work.\n\nGot it! Yeah, using it the way you described, it worked really well. I will stick to it; as for the multi-key was just an idea/question, I'm fine also using the `<C-r>` keys in both OS, Thanks for creating those amazing plugins 🏅 \n\n",
