        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> if the copied line includes a specific number on it, for example: If I copy `app/models/user.rb:10` it won't take me to that line in the `.rb` file.\n> \n> Is it possible to add that feature in the plugin?\n\nAll pasting into prompt does is adds text to the prompt. It will behave the same way as user manually types those characters, which in turn means that matched items will be updated according to the new query. If there is an item that matches `app/models/user.rb:10` (which is not the case with default pickers; the closest are `grep` and `grep_live`, but they use custom separator between path and line number), then it will be shown in matches; otherwise - it won't.",
