        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I'd like to say it worked but it didn't.\n\nYet it did work: `nvim/.config/nvim/init.lua` *did* get pasted into prompt and extended query (as if user typed all that string manually). This resulted into no items selected because there is item matching `nvim/.config/nvim/init.lua` query.\n\nThere seems to be a confusion about what `:Pick files` does. It 1) populates items with all file paths in the target directory (as decided by the `rg` CLI tool); and 2) allows user to pick one/many to open by narrowing down items via query.\n\nIf you expect 'nvim/.config/nvim/init.lua' file to be present in the initial list of items, then [configuring `rg` might help](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/307221b90376b68fc7e007e9315836370e9efb8f/doc/mini-pick.txt#L80-L85). For example, adding `--hidden` option to `rg` might help (here is [how I do it](https://github.com/echasnovski/dotfiles/blob/master/ripgrep/.config/ripgrep/.ripgreprc) in my dotfiles).\n\nAnd again, appending `:40` will not magically act as \"go to line 40\" in `:Pick files`. It will only narrow down items that match query with `:40` added.",
